        "content": "*(The world resolves around you, crisp and bright as a freshly painted miniature. You stand at a crossroads just outside the humble village of Oakhaven. The air smells of damp earth and baking bread. A weathered signpost points three ways: to the forest path (marked with a crude wolf carving), the mountain road (a chipped sword symbol), and the King's Highway (a faded crown).)*\n\n**Narrator:** *(A clear, calm voice, speaking directly into your mind)* So. This is where it begins, Ray of Oakhaven. Eighteen summers old, a head full of ballads, and a heart itching for the weight of a sword. The village elder says you have the makings of a guardsman. Your mother wishes you’d take up the blacksmith’s hammer. But you hear a different call. The question is… which path will you answer first?\n\n*(A breeze rustles the leaves, carrying the distant sound of a merchant’s cart on the King’s Highway, and a faint, unsettling howl from the deep forest.)*",
